As the Keeper of Knowledge, Focauld resided in the [[Cloisters]] in [[New York]], guarding the ancient tomes of the [[Casterwill family]] that details the hidden hiding places of the scattered family members. {{source|The Casterwill Connection}}

After the [[Blood Spiral]] found Focauld's location, he used the power [[Knowledgelock]] to seal the tomes' info into a single [[Cypherdex]] Crystal. After alerting [[Teien Casterwill]] of his situation, he held off against [[Kiel]], [[Marduk]] and the [[Casterwill Hunters]] before being joined and rescued by [[Sophie Casterwill]] and her [[Huntik Foundation]] team. However, he stubbornly refused to welcome her into the family's secrets. {{source|The Casterwill Connection}}

Outside the Cloisters, Focauld witnessed the Blue Star of [[Quetzalcoatl]], activated by [[Lok Lambert]], signalling the Casterwill family to come out of hiding. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

After joining his family in the [[Fortress of Iron Will]], Focauld, like [[Lucas Casterwill]], voted against Sophie's demands to fight the Blood Spiral and instead ensure the preservation of the Casterwills by hiding and surviving. {{source|Sophie on Trial}} After Sophie returned from the Trial of Courage with [[Mythras]], the Titan of Valor, Focauld was still opposed to fighting the Spirals. During the Spiral army's attack on Iron Will, Focauld remained inside and helped the 5 [[Rune Guardian|Rue Guardians]] in activating the Fortress' defenses and summoning the [[Coralgolem]], [[Feyone]] and [[Icarus]] Titans. Following their victory and the death of [[Nimue]], Focauld told Sophie that she had given him something to believe in again. {{source|The Spiral War}}

During the final battle against [[the Betrayer]] at the [[Blood Spiral Base]], Focuald travelled in a [[Scramjet]] with the other Casterwills. {{source|The Spiral War}} Focauld was seen elated at the defeat of the Betrayer. {{Source|Dante's Return}}

